From 456a7c5896a2a7e873a01359b6132cc41519e2e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pedro Alves <pedro@palves.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:46:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use UCRT's own wcrtomb() and wctomb()

Backport of the change from upstream snapshot 20260822, by Liu Hao:

  > improve wide-character support with UCRT (patches by Liu Hao)
    + use UCRT's wcrtomb rather than _nc_wctomb

For MinGW, curses.priv.h replaces the C library's multibyte functions
with ncurses' own: mbtowc(), mblen(), wctomb() and wcrtomb() become
macros over _nc_mbtowc(), _nc_mblen() and _nc_wctomb(), as MinGW's
wide-character functions "do not work correctly".  That was true of
msvcrt, not of UCRT.

With current mingw-w64 headers the macros also break the build.
curses.h includes <wchar.h> only when NEED_WCHAR_H is set, which
configure decides by checking whether mbstate_t is declared without it.
mingw-w64 commit 8c4baed92d4d ("headers: crt: define mbstate_t in
corecrt.h") moved mbstate_t to <corecrt.h>, which <stdlib.h> includes,
so NEED_WCHAR_H comes out 0, and <wchar.h> is included after the
macros.  The wcrtomb() macro then turns its declaration of wcrtomb()
into a second, conflicting declaration of _nc_wctomb():

  curses.priv.h:2300:25: error: conflicting types for '_nc_wctomb'; have 'size_t(char * restrict,  wchar_t)'

Upstream skips the whole replacement under UCRT, both the macros in
curses.priv.h and the definitions of the _nc_ functions in widechars.c,
so the C runtime's own four functions are used and nothing is renamed.
This patch makes the same two changes as the upstream snapshot.  The
UCRT64 toolchain defines _UCRT.  Drop this patch once the bundled
ncurses includes 20260822.
---
 ncurses/curses.priv.h        | 2 +-
 ncurses/widechar/widechars.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ncurses/curses.priv.h b/ncurses/curses.priv.h
index 8999ecd..e14bec7 100644
--- a/ncurses/curses.priv.h
+++ b/ncurses/curses.priv.h
@@ -2291,7 +2291,7 @@ extern NCURSES_EXPORT(int) _nc_eventlist_timeout(_nc_eventlist *);
  */
 #if USE_WIDEC_SUPPORT
 
-#if defined(_NC_WINDOWS_NATIVE) && !defined(_NC_MSC) && !USE_NAMED_PIPES
+#if defined(_NC_WINDOWS_NATIVE) && !defined(_NC_MSC) && !USE_NAMED_PIPES && !defined(_UCRT)
 /*
  * MinGW has wide-character functions, but they do not work correctly.
  */
diff --git a/ncurses/widechar/widechars.c b/ncurses/widechar/widechars.c
index 6ea008d..14f46a1 100644
--- a/ncurses/widechar/widechars.c
+++ b/ncurses/widechar/widechars.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 
 MODULE_ID("$Id: widechars.c,v 1.11 2025/02/20 01:02:09 tom Exp $")
 
-#if defined(_NC_MINGW)
+#if defined(_NC_MINGW) && !defined(_UCRT)
 /*
  * MinGW has wide-character functions, but they do not work correctly.
  */
-- 
